# PR#15: correct in general and answered the way the finding itself allows, by requiring
# a context-aware source rather than pretending a wrapper can interrupt a read. Nothing
# outside a read can end one that has already entered a syscall: a goroutine plus a select
# returns from Put while the abandoned read goes on writing into a temporary file the
# caller is about to remove, which trades a stall for a corruption. The requirement is
# stated on Put, and both callers this has satisfy it — whatsmeow's download hands over
# bytes already in memory, and an HTTP body from a request carrying the context unblocks
# when the context does. The check before each read is what covers a source that yields.
